{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5954d6bc189fcd6a5b067571dcd7f28f72aeb338642c7355d7f2948fadc819c0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we establish some relationships between the topoi\nassociated to these sites.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1180215722ae63882047268b44a72225f372a791bf36a874a5e1330a20dd47d", "unit_id": "tag:0DBC:prose-0008"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : T \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nu : (\\Sch/T)_{ph} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/S)_{ph},\n\\quad\nV/T \\longmapsto V/S\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nv : (\\Sch/S)_{ph} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/T)_{ph},\n\\quad\n(U \\to S) \\longmapsto (U \\times_S T \\to T).\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_{big} :\n\\Sh((\\Sch/T)_{ph})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Sh((\\Sch/S)_{ph})\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f_{big}^{-1}(\\mathcal{G})(U/T) = \\mathcal{G}(U/S)$", "MATH_0008": "$f_{big, *}(\\mathcal{F})(U/S) = \\mathcal{F}(U \\times_S T/T)$", "MATH_0009": "$f_{big}^{-1}$", "MATH_0010": "$f_{big!}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-big-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:671829621ed42df27422d55efa3ea44d3920c5ce701a8f378c9c1e22cbb7bcfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c6abe80cd518555bd675d5fd97268521f003d3699f3a22a2de1ecdfedb4ba3b2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a big ph site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism in <MATH_0003>.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0004>\nis cocontinuous, and has a continuous right adjoint\n<MATH_0005>\nThey induce the same morphism of topoi\n<MATH_0006>\nWe have <MATH_0007>.\nWe have <MATH_0008>.\nAlso, <MATH_0009> has a left adjoint <MATH_0010> which commutes with\nfibre products and equalizers.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:479c0d279db749fb03c6a17145d13566cbba9703ca9e735e56c5a4f98caaf404", "unit_id": "tag:0DBR:statement"}
